[{"id":"VRCE-4-6-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":1,"english":"Sugrīva well pleased again addressed Rāghava, the son of Raghu, saying, O Rāma, this servant of thine, foremost of my counsellors, Hanumān, has related (to me), the reason of your arrival in this lone forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9a45be4c2df7c67f81924dc124443992a67011562dba582ad2ed537d14a03b03","compact":"6f94bf5cf49ceeb6903755ced915b1469b88a39707257ad8121b9523de93ffa1","nasal":"a111043a9bb329974ad5c0e033bcb158606ffd6b60b6aa583fff291e098a5279"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":2,"english":"Your wife, Maithili, daughter to Janaka, separated from you as well as the intelligent Laksmana, and weeping (in consequence) was carried off by a Rākṣa. Seeing for opportunities of doing mischief that Rākşa, having slain Jațáyu, has caused to you the grief that comes of separation from one's wife.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"070549ed25953d4c7098ba62d4c288882a0b41da41b75c160e584727504efe09","compact":"b39a5e1cb9b9891773051720512ea2baf4b8472c313bfb1a235ad1f990ca69b5","nasal":"b39a5e1cb9b9891773051720512ea2baf4b8472c313bfb1a235ad1f990ca69b5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":3,"english":"Your wife, Maithili, daughter to Janaka, separated from you as well as the intelligent Laksmana, and weeping (in consequence) was carried off by a Rākṣa. Seeing for opportunities of doing mischief that Rākşa, having slain Jațáyu, has caused to you the grief that comes of separation from one's wife.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01a665c3b6fbdd0f1cf43191737770c3d8b1e79614aa99040787c6eaeec80ad8","compact":"aedb15a74e3a0e18a16ac87477f2773dd15451ad325ed771a5d1d4f38e194315","nasal":"13c077dbba87368e9fa5a02602b08adb2fb9ab6c0194ba123e3518ea2211c0f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":4,"english":"But you with soon be relieved from the sorrow that comes of separation from one's wife. Her will I bring like to the ravished Devasruti.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.926,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec2f293cadf0efdba4bd33c9fab8504aa7e62274a4775ff44f3843f020abf203","compact":"8c3aaccb2c13e24658363c84513cbd39db1f5488b3854b99d3a9a8e876f6b865","nasal":"8c3aaccb2c13e24658363c84513cbd39db1f5488b3854b99d3a9a8e876f6b865"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":5,"english":"O repressor of foes, whether she be in the nether regions or under the sky, I will, bringing your wife, make her over to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69e507106593a03589ddcfd55eb2c47cb9593e07668fb391dbdd1f289d346aed","compact":"0480b3e0ec99feb9b7e3e944b7fb3c659aafe6e419138df5ee65636472e7f8fe","nasal":"98f45f3c8447fab650f02f0b0de667b4d5b7c2616f2a11972ec88456c1b2e03b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":6,"english":"O Rāghava, know my words to be true. O mighty-armed one, like to poison, your wife is incapable of being digested even by the gods and Asuras with Indra (at their head). O mightyarmed one, leave off sorrow, I will bring back your beloved.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"361c1d893b4315ae27af5313be3e8ffc52de04e7cfd5dc93b491e053939ff7b8","compact":"b61a8d1ec88e00141accad3701a302869233b788e4008f4ca038900dfc735d20","nasal":"ed9aedd6b66aae8ae8cb8cbaed990c262320056131d28a6b90457f7237f905bc"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":7,"english":"From guess I find that it was doubtless Mithilā's daughter whom I saw when she was being carried away by that Räksa of terrific deeds. She was crying, Rama, Laksmana, Laks maņa,' and in the lap of Răvaņa she looked like the wife of the Snake-chief.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d2bd0ac5de683a574a76a704a20bff76115a87ae281bec56b21dc40022811c1","compact":"c832d777717c1b56f3457b7f3679bce1f67e5f62bddecb5451b9a47ea24104a9","nasal":"c832d777717c1b56f3457b7f3679bce1f67e5f62bddecb5451b9a47ea24104a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":8,"english":"From guess I find that it was doubtless Mithilā's daughter whom I saw when she was being carried away by that Räksa of terrific deeds. She was crying, Rama, Laksmana, Laks maņa,' and in the lap of Răvaņa she looked like the wife of the Snake-chief.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3bb1cd2085b394b855c80b7276bfc00ab3b34b5113b361ddc76e2d1db6dc02a0","compact":"5812a37558608c413d094af356fce5b2b2fbdcb0417b3eb2766fe15bb4cd6ee0","nasal":"a2d3ae97fd0f3e74902880da39c0628af4aae0aeb9f4905ddfeac2de4d948091"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":9,"english":"Seeing me along with my four counsellors stationed at the hill, she dropped down her scarf and her ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5546851a9213b2b20aa70543a52de419c0c71ff41ad69c88294ec0aeceeb737b","compact":"b3e289e4011bb916e13a9c65d864211cd55d04cf65ecc063ce7b661eea79d910","nasal":"e2f82e7ef4ebbc4b1cca092620891aeb2342c890715041377f3fc2f672e640af"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":10,"english":"All these, O Rāghava, I have taken and kept (with me). I will bring them. It behoveth you to recognise them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26bcba4be1be172764b9cd78577331f97e38e44a0af7594654a607f52abbc699","compact":"60d379ed1daac341e39943b93aed71d2c483f7e1e189df88c0b376419544b110","nasal":"60d379ed1daac341e39943b93aed71d2c483f7e1e189df88c0b376419544b110"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":11,"english":"There upon Rāma spoke to the sweetspeeched Sugrīva, 'Bring (them), at once, my friend. Why did you tarry?'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1ad5fb87de1e74b7478c6985cee56fbaaace578632115da326bfcaf63153ac1f","compact":"132e2e0ab16e807c706ce0b706bbce06893f66c4388c4a6fd9d582a56bdc8175","nasal":"7970b7d3fa7ef926e7f9230a70d4e65759199b1c9b33da9227e82583a2f78b00"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":12,"english":"Having been thus addressed, Sugrīva swiftly entered a deep cavern in the mountain, with the view of doing what was dear to Rāghava. Then taking the scarf as well as the ornaments. Look at this, (Saying this) the monkey held them before Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3cf219eb8d23f431ffd36e15e9316edda7fc9f78bf8d17d98a4848117503c467","compact":"b0e024986a374c43205c63a1127bc944adb2da5b0c9ccb7a22736389d12ebbab","nasal":"0687a7b8ae303b8595d6aa48c5188e6d16065f4435479d13e80dda71eb77bf8c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-6-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":6,"verse":13,"english":"Having been thus addressed, Sugrīva swiftly entered a deep cavern in the mountain, with the view of doing what was dear to Rāghava. Then taking the scarf as well as the ornaments. Look at this, (Saying this) the monkey held them before Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.673,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-6-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4006013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3eaef5cff5e1d62f9c3aac9545383978d4d62ce37961cfa549e95b9b8d308368","compact":"42ee93c4e5a7795f236e4fd7c85a9b5af8d18c7cd6343598119208a052044db9","nasal":"42ee93c4e5a7795f236e4fd7c